Z||000000||DaveL||01-24-2001||09:45 AM||||After reading some good articles on it, I decided to switch to full synthetic oil. From what I read, most additives are a waste of money, full synthetic provides the best possible lubrication and protection. I switched to Valvoline full synthetic, and haven't had any problems or changes in consumption. But I have seen a few references here alluding to the possibility of negative effects from the change....Is that True?? Has anyone experienced this?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tom Philips||01-25-2001||07:28 AM||||With everything i have read and the testing that has been done all the info says not to waste your money on using synthetics the lubricating qualities are the same, the claim to fame for synthetics is it can take high temperatures without breaking down...||||reg||1
